  "final_message": "I'm checking the repository status and codebase structure.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why This Cannot Be Removed Directly\n\n1. **External Contract Compatibility**: Even if `orders-service` does not read `channel` internally, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) events are published across repository boundaries to downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` is a breaking schema change that would break deployed consumers.\n2. **Model Dependency**: Because [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) constructs the event from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29), the domain model must retain [`channel`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L23) so valid, backward-compatible events can continue to be emitted.\n\n### Required Deprecation Workflow\n\nTo safely sunset `channel` in compliance with ARCH-4:\n\n1. **Mark as Deprecated**: Annotate `channel` with `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L23).\n2. **Coordinate with Consumers**: Notify the maintainers of `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` to ensure they migrate away from reading the field.\n3. **Schema Evolution**: Once external consumers have migrated, follow the cross-service schema evolution policy (e.g., make the field optional or bump `schemaVersion`) before removing it entirely.\n",
